From: Yureka Lilian <yureka@cyberchaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: nvme: Add apple,t8132-nvme-ans2 compatible

Backport of 9dbada7ebff2bb68f4f1e44450c728b86805703b, moving the unchanged
new compatible past this kernel's already present t8122 enum. Runtime
NVMe and ANS register resources are unchanged by this binding patch.
Source: https://cyberchaos.dev/yuka/linux/-/commit/9dbada7ebff2bb68f4f1e44450c728b86805703b

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvme/apple,nvme-ans.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvme/apple,nvme-ans.yaml
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
   compatible:
     oneOf:
       - const: apple,t8015-nvme-ans2
+      - const: apple,t8132-nvme-ans2
       - items:
           - enum:
               - apple,t6020-nvme-ans2
